  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 24.67,
      "end": 55.84,
      "text": "on 275 and 285 and in stereo on vhf this is national radio one hi i'm thomas the vance and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.84,
      "end": 62.74,
      "text": "welcome to this classic edition of the friday rock show tonight three sets by jimmy hendrix",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.74,
      "end": 66.86,
      "text": "the late and much-missed wizard of the guitar we've got nine numbers by jimmy plus his famous",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.86,
      "end": 72.44,
      "text": "radio one jingle and a jam that just happened when stevie wonder one day popped into the studio",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.44,
      "end": 91.58,
      "text": "you'll hear classic cuts by the band brand x and the doors among others new cuts from judy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 91.58,
      "end": 95.4,
      "text": "Zouk, Ian Dury, Robert Palmer, the Ohio Players, and The Doors.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 95.76,
      "end": 97.2,
      "text": "And don't forget the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.52,
      "end": 100.08,
      "text": "Maybe tonight you get yourself a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.14,
      "end": 103.76,
      "text": "But tonight we start with a classic.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.62,
      "end": 108.22,
      "text": "Nice bit of boogie that was.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.22,
      "end": 691.44,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 696.44,
      "end": 698.16,
      "text": "That was called Further On Up The Road.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 698.26,
      "end": 701.16,
      "text": "Of course, it came from the big album's set called The Last Dwarf,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 701.18,
      "end": 703.3,
      "text": "and it was played by the band featuring Mr. Eric Clapton.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 703.86,
      "end": 706.42,
      "text": "And we played especially for a gentleman by the name of Carl Maidment,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 706.42,
      "end": 709.88,
      "text": "who's a Finisterre block, HMS Collingwood, Ferrum Enhance,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 709.88,
      "end": 712.12,
      "text": "who wants me to say to a good friend of his",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 712.12,
      "end": 714.94,
      "text": "by the name of Angela Morgan of Habersham Street in Cardiff",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 714.94,
      "end": 716.48,
      "text": "that she's the bestest gal ever.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 716.92,
      "end": 720.49,
      "text": "You can still share the T-shirts any time you like.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 720.49,
      "end": 720.84,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 723.8,
      "end": 725.72,
      "text": "And before that, you heard one of the real classics,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 725.84,
      "end": 727.5,
      "text": "the Blue Oyster Cult and Don't Fear the Reaper.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 727.72,
      "end": 729.56,
      "text": "For a gentleman who's all of 14 years of age",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 729.56,
      "end": 731.12,
      "text": "and who happens to like this programme,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 731.22,
      "end": 732.58,
      "text": "see, they're not all geriatric, you know.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 733.04,
      "end": 734.64,
      "text": "That's James Brown I'm talking about",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 734.64,
      "end": 738.36,
      "text": "at the Old Vicarage Church Road Grange-over-Sands in Cumbria.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 738.92,
      "end": 741.8,
      "text": "And also for Alan Fazekaly of Sherbourne,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 741.8,
      "end": 742.86,
      "text": "who likes BOC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 743.18,
      "end": 749.44,
      "text": "And this is Judy Zouk.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 749.66,
      "end": 752.66,
      "text": "Quite amazing, really.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 752.66,
      "end": 1261.16,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1261.16,
      "end": 1263.32,
      "text": "When that album first came out, a lot of people heard it and thought,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1263.42,
      "end": 1266.08,
      "text": "oh, not really the same as the man used to be.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1266.46,
      "end": 1270.12,
      "text": "But it's gone straight into the charts at number two and well deserves to do so.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1270.26,
      "end": 1271.48,
      "text": "The album's called Do It Yourself,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1271.7,
      "end": 1274.9,
      "text": "and it features the amazing artistry of Ian Dury and the Blockheads,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1274.98,
      "end": 1276.48,
      "text": "and that track was entitled Don't Ask Me.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1276.98,
      "end": 1280.78,
      "text": "Before that, you heard Ray Worley playing the saxophone on a track entitled Katera Island.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1281.44,
      "end": 1283.22,
      "text": "It's from a new LP that's out on Rocket.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1283.44,
      "end": 1285.08,
      "text": "The album's called Welcome to the Cruise,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1285.56,
      "end": 1287.46,
      "text": "and it features the talent of Judy Zouk,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1287.46,
      "end": 1291.72,
      "text": "who wants me to dedicate that record to Denny Godber, who does her hair,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1292.16,
      "end": 1297.14,
      "text": "and was also seen, here's a bit of scandal, this afternoon, making Rod even blonder.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1298.06,
      "end": 1300.74,
      "text": "And this should be a little jingle, but it isn't.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1301.04,
      "end": 1302.62,
      "text": "Never mind. Forget the jingle.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1303.44,
      "end": 1307.08,
      "text": "Because I really just wanted to say, ladies and gentlemen, Jimi Hendrix.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1335.79,
      "end": 1338.79,
      "text": "Hear that again?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1338.79,
      "end": 2133.6,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2138.6,
      "end": 2142.22,
      "text": "Foxy Lady, Love or Confusion, Hey Joe and Stone Free,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2142.46,
      "end": 2146.92,
      "text": "as recorded on the 13th of the 2nd, 1967, by Jimi Hendrix.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2152.27,
      "end": 2154.89,
      "text": "Stacks of people have written in to hear sessions by Hendrix,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2154.99,
      "end": 2156.41,
      "text": "so I'll just mention a few people.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2156.49,
      "end": 2158.55,
      "text": "Gordon Hobson of Hazel Grove in Stockport,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2158.87,
      "end": 2161.01,
      "text": "Paul Waddington of Forest Hill in Newcastle,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2161.39,
      "end": 2164.95,
      "text": "Per Vees Khan of [redacted address], Chelmsford in Essex,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2164.95,
      "end": 2167.57,
      "text": "Craig Morrison and somebody by the name of Neil",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2167.57,
      "end": 2171.15,
      "text": "[redacted address], Cheadle Hume in Cheshire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2171.15,
      "end": 2175.21,
      "text": "and A. Gibson at [redacted address] in Worcester",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2175.21,
      "end": 2179.66,
      "text": "More Hendrix later",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2179.66,
      "end": 2181.42,
      "text": "It's 25 minutes now before 11",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2181.42,
      "end": 2183.3,
      "text": "Tone and I were in the office this afternoon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2183.3,
      "end": 2185.88,
      "text": "and we thought, let's bung a few singles in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2185.88,
      "end": 2186.76,
      "text": "So we have",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2186.76,
      "end": 2189.76,
      "text": "That band, they're so inventive",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2189.76,
      "end": 2695.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2718.11,
      "end": 2720.91,
      "text": "That's the new single that's just come out on Virgin by Devo",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2720.91,
      "end": 2723.65,
      "text": "and it's entitled The Day My Baby Gave Me a Surprise",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2724.39,
      "end": 2726.27,
      "text": "And before that, something that's been lifted from the album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2726.27,
      "end": 2729.03,
      "text": "called Secrets by Robert Palmer, issued as a single on Island.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2729.15,
      "end": 2730.79,
      "text": "It's called A Bad Case of Loving You.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2731.23,
      "end": 2733.41,
      "text": "Doctor, Doctor, that's a real good record as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2733.79,
      "end": 2734.27,
      "text": "Good single.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2734.45,
      "end": 2736.93,
      "text": "Girls in Action, you heard before that by the Invaders.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2737.05,
      "end": 2737.99,
      "text": "That's come out on Polydor.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2738.25,
      "end": 2740.07,
      "text": "And it's a Jimmy Percy production.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2740.53,
      "end": 2741.57,
      "text": "Nice one, Jim.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2742.07,
      "end": 2753.1,
      "text": "Hi, this is Al Matthews, the new man about discovating from Saturday Week.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2753.36,
      "end": 2756.64,
      "text": "This week, though, they've booked me to give you the rundown on the holiday weekend.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2756.64,
      "end": 2759.58,
      "text": "And what a great Radio 1 weekend we've got for you.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2759.58,
      "end": 2762.08,
      "text": "All your regular favorites on Saturday and Sunday,",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2762.36,
      "end": 2766.38,
      "text": "plus two hours of Tina Turner with her own star choice in stereo",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2766.38,
      "end": 2768.46,
      "text": "at 7 o'clock Sunday evening.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2768.6,
      "end": 2768.98,
      "text": "Monday.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2769.72,
      "end": 2774.04,
      "text": "At 11.30, Tony Blackburn takes the road show to the Surrey County show at Guilford.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2774.36,
      "end": 2778.4,
      "text": "At 1.30, Billy Connolly presents the Connolly Collection of his music.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2778.64,
      "end": 2783.66,
      "text": "And at 5.30, the first ever live relay of Elton John's concert direct from Moscow.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2784.0,
      "end": 2786.78,
      "text": "It's a weekend when you can't afford not to have a radio round.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2787.04,
      "end": 2788.34,
      "text": "Make sure it's tuned to.",
      "source": "Al Matthews"
    },
    {
      "start": 2788.34,
      "end": 2809.72,
      "text": "earlier than usual quarter to 11 the friday night connection loads of mail this week in turn and i",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2809.72,
      "end": 2812.72,
      "text": "were trying to figure out whether you thought it was easy or whether you thought it was so hard",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2812.72,
      "end": 2816.44,
      "text": "you'd have a crack at it anyway but you really did send in a lot of mail and we thank you very",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2816.44,
      "end": 2821.98,
      "text": "much indeed every letter does get read but i have to tell you the winner right now so some people",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2821.98,
      "end": 2827.44,
      "text": "are going to be disappointed the man who gets the 10 pound record token is mike duffield at number",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2827.44,
      "end": 2834.24,
      "text": "[redacted address] university of bath down there in bath in avon and he wrote dear friday rock show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2834.24,
      "end": 2839.62,
      "text": "the friday night connection for the 19th of may was that the lyrics of each track included the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2839.62,
      "end": 2846.28,
      "text": "title of the album from which they came those albums otherwise not having a title track in the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2846.28,
      "end": 2853.0,
      "text": "usual sense mike you're right and the tracks that we played were dancing with the moonlight night",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2853.0,
      "end": 2859.72,
      "text": "the genesis brain damage and eclipse by the pink floyd and listen learn and read on by deep purple",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2859.72,
      "end": 2868.67,
      "text": "and the albums were selling england by the pound dark side of the moon and the book of talisen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2868.67,
      "end": 2880.36,
      "text": "and now let me tell you that mr mike duffield has put together a friday night connection himself",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2880.36,
      "end": 2886.84,
      "text": "which is quite arty and quite clever and quite becoming of a university student lecturer maybe",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2886.84,
      "end": 2891.88,
      "text": "see if you can figure out what the connection is between these three pieces of music",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2891.88,
      "end": 2897.28,
      "text": "That's what I call an inventive choice of music",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2897.28,
      "end": 3868.19,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3868.19,
      "end": 3870.81,
      "text": "And that last track I haven't heard since it came out",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3870.81,
      "end": 3872.31,
      "text": "And it's still weird",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3872.31,
      "end": 3876.96,
      "text": "And that was our Friday Night Connection for this week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3876.96,
      "end": 3878.22,
      "text": "Put together by Mike Duffield",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3878.22,
      "end": 3880.78,
      "text": "At [redacted address], University of Bath",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3880.78,
      "end": 3881.66,
      "text": "Down there in Avon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3881.66,
      "end": 3884.04,
      "text": "Get yourself a £10 record token, Mike",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3884.04,
      "end": 3884.68,
      "text": "Congratulations",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3884.68,
      "end": 3893.6,
      "text": "And just listening to that triptych there",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3893.6,
      "end": 3894.98,
      "text": "It's really difficult",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3894.98,
      "end": 3896.42,
      "text": "The answer to this is difficult",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3896.42,
      "end": 3897.62,
      "text": "I wish you the best of luck",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3897.62,
      "end": 3899.38,
      "text": "Send your answers to the Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3899.38,
      "end": 3901.15,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3901.77,
      "end": 3905.89,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1, London, W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3906.75,
      "end": 3910.35,
      "text": "And don't forget, along with the answer, or what you think the answer is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3910.69,
      "end": 3913.27,
      "text": "you've got to put together your own Friday night connection as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3913.73,
      "end": 3917.09,
      "text": "Three pieces of music that have a theme or a connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3917.71,
      "end": 3919.59,
      "text": "It can be hard or it can be easy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3921.97,
      "end": 3928.84,
      "text": "It's four minutes now past 11 o'clock.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3929.22,
      "end": 3930.36,
      "text": "This is Funky.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3930.86,
      "end": 3933.86,
      "text": "Type of track there.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4546.66,
      "end": 4549.3,
      "text": "It's by Ron Wood from his solo album that's just come out on CBS.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4549.3,
      "end": 4551.04,
      "text": "Yes, the album's called Give Me Some Neck.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4551.53,
      "end": 4553.33,
      "text": "And the track there was called We All Get Old.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4553.43,
      "end": 4554.93,
      "text": "Indeed we do, but gracefully.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4555.47,
      "end": 4557.51,
      "text": "And before that, you heard something by the Ohio Players.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4558.25,
      "end": 4559.35,
      "text": "Yes, they really were.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4559.49,
      "end": 4560.81,
      "text": "It's on Arista, their album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4560.93,
      "end": 4562.09,
      "text": "It's called Everybody Up.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4562.39,
      "end": 4566.07,
      "text": "And the title of the track is Take Defunk Off, Fly.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4566.57,
      "end": 4568.15,
      "text": "Or if you like, Take Defunk Off, Fly.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4568.83,
      "end": 4573.03,
      "text": "On Radio 1, this Sunday evening at 7 o'clock, it's Star Special.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4573.35,
      "end": 4574.43,
      "text": "Hi, this is Tina Turner.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4574.43,
      "end": 4577.41,
      "text": "And this Sunday, I'll be playing two hours of my favorite music",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4577.41,
      "end": 4579.61,
      "text": "right here on your favorite radio station.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4580.25,
      "end": 4581.27,
      "text": "You've got to be there.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4581.55,
      "end": 4582.15,
      "text": "You've got to listen.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4582.35,
      "end": 4583.17,
      "text": "You've got to stay with me.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4583.27,
      "end": 4585.57,
      "text": "You've got to hear how fantastic I am.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4585.83,
      "end": 4591.75,
      "text": "Tima Turner, 7 o'clock this Sunday on 275-285 and Stereo VHS.",
      "source": "Tina Turner"
    },
    {
      "start": 4595.62,
      "end": 4596.48,
      "text": "At 11.15.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4596.58,
      "end": 4597.06,
      "text": "Thanks, Andy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4597.14,
      "end": 4599.98,
      "text": "Have a nice time over there in Moscow introducing Mr. Elton John.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4600.1,
      "end": 4602.6,
      "text": "I think it's at 5.30 on Monday here on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4602.6,
      "end": 4608.04,
      "text": "And now, for Top Gear, this was recorded on the 24th of the 12th of 1967.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4608.94,
      "end": 4610.36,
      "text": "More Jimi Hendrix.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4617.7,
      "end": 4626.31,
      "text": "Radio One, you're the only one for me.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4641.44,
      "end": 4645.83,
      "text": "Just turn that dial, make your music worthwhile.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4647.51,
      "end": 4655.85,
      "text": "Radio One, you stole my gal, but I love you just the same.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4657.23,
      "end": 4662.63,
      "text": "Sunshine of your love, Hey Joe and Voodoo Child.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4662.63,
      "end": 5183.1,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5183.1,
      "end": 5185.82,
      "text": "To the best of our knowledge, they've never been put out on radio before,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5185.82,
      "end": 5189.08,
      "text": "but aficionados of Jimi Hendrix will certainly know where they came from.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5189.62,
      "end": 5192.08,
      "text": "And before that, the amazing jingle that he put together for Top Gear",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5192.08,
      "end": 5194.5,
      "text": "way back on the 24th of the 1267.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5194.8,
      "end": 5197.5,
      "text": "That was Christmas Eve, and I remember doing that programme now.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5198.06,
      "end": 5201.64,
      "text": "We found something here that we think also has never been broadcast on radio.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5202.16,
      "end": 5204.52,
      "text": "It's Jimi Hendrix and Stevie Wonder,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5204.8,
      "end": 5208.2,
      "text": "and we think possibly the title of the piece of music is In the Midnight Hour,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5208.32,
      "end": 5210.78,
      "text": "but essentially it's just a jam.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5210.78,
      "end": 5509.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5509.02,
      "end": 5511.34,
      "text": "That's Stevie Wonder on drums and Jimi Hendrix on the guitar.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5511.34,
      "end": 5513.92,
      "text": "and In the Midnight Hour and I Was Born to Love Her",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5513.92,
      "end": 5515.92,
      "text": "and all sort of jumble up things like that.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5516.0,
      "end": 5518.76,
      "text": "A real jam recorded purely by chance",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5518.76,
      "end": 5521.48,
      "text": "in a studio on the 6th or the 10th of 1967.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5522.54,
      "end": 5524.66,
      "text": "And we'd like to thank everybody who helped us",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5524.66,
      "end": 5527.94,
      "text": "to find those pieces of music by the late Mr Hendricks.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5528.28,
      "end": 5529.36,
      "text": "We appreciate it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5530.0,
      "end": 5533.38,
      "text": "And now for something entirely different by Brand X.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5580.0,
      "end": 5935.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5940.0,
      "end": 6197.52,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6197.52,
      "end": 6198.56,
      "text": "And writers on the storm.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6198.74,
      "end": 6200.52,
      "text": "That's for a gentleman by the name of Tony Harvey",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6200.52,
      "end": 6202.94,
      "text": "who's doing a stretch at the moment in Aberdeen Prison.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6203.3,
      "end": 6204.28,
      "text": "Tony, get yourself out.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6204.28,
      "end": 6211.04,
      "text": "legally and don't get yourself back in again and also for kevin guy of number 16 stonely drive",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6211.04,
      "end": 6217.56,
      "text": "i think it's catherton possibly in oxen and before that you heard the track called black moon by",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6217.56,
      "end": 6222.78,
      "text": "brand x from the op masks and that was for everybody at desborough school in maidenhead",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6222.78,
      "end": 6229.07,
      "text": "who are doing exams at the moment and anybody servicing a typewriter and also for jerry henderson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6229.07,
      "end": 6232.29,
      "text": "of number [redacted address], Kildrum,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6232.69,
      "end": 6233.93,
      "text": "in Cumbernauld in Scotland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6242.1,
      "end": 6243.48,
      "text": "Now let's get back to Jimi Hendrix.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6243.56,
      "end": 6246.68,
      "text": "This was recorded on the 17th of the 10th, 1967.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6494.1,
      "end": 6497.0,
      "text": "He's gonna be a son of a gun.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6507.61,
      "end": 6508.59,
      "text": "The world's gonna know.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7147.38,
      "end": 7149.06,
      "text": "The late Jimi Hendrix and Driving South.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7149.18,
      "end": 7150.3,
      "text": "Before that, Hoochie Coochie Man,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7150.34,
      "end": 7151.38,
      "text": "and before that, Can You Please?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7151.48,
      "end": 7152.42,
      "text": "Come Crawl Out Your Window.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7152.58,
      "end": 7154.18,
      "text": "And that was our classic session tonight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7154.18,
      "end": 7156.6,
      "text": "from a classic, classic man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7156.6,
      "end": 7308.06,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7313.06,
      "end": 7314.4,
      "text": "Alice Cooper and School's Out,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7314.4,
      "end": 7316.36,
      "text": "and that's our last number tonight on the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7316.46,
      "end": 7318.24,
      "text": "Many thanks to everybody who assisted us",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7318.24,
      "end": 7319.84,
      "text": "in finding those Jimi Hendrix tapes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7319.9,
      "end": 7321.08,
      "text": "and we trust that you enjoyed them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7322.04,
      "end": 7324.46,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show is a Tony Wilson production.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7325.85,
      "end": 7327.33,
      "text": "Our engineer tonight was Mark.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7327.37,
      "end": 7327.87,
      "text": "Thank you, Mark.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7328.29,
      "end": 7329.33,
      "text": "On Rock On tomorrow,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7329.55,
      "end": 7332.15,
      "text": "we're going to be previewing the Nick Lowe album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7332.39,
      "end": 7333.65,
      "text": "the new Nick Lowe album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7333.65,
      "end": 7337.17,
      "text": "That's on Rock On tomorrow at 4 o'clock on Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7337.85,
      "end": 7341.59,
      "text": "Next week, two hours of Yes in concert from Wembley.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7342.32,
      "end": 7343.3,
      "text": "Wherever you are,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7343.84,
      "end": 7346.22,
      "text": "hope you're warm and comfortable and feeling okay.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7346.44,
      "end": 7347.06,
      "text": "I'll see you tomorrow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7347.28,
      "end": 7362.53,
      "text": "Well then, God bless you.",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}